{"type":"message","id":"d8bf912e","parentId":"31957a77","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:50:22.756Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should note that Z input now returns an aware datetime instead of naive, and explicit offsets like +02:00 are now preserved as aware values rather than being converted to UTC.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`. It now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime` with a fixed format. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass, including `test_dates`.\n\n**Cause:** the old format `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"` had no slot for the trailing `Z`, so `strptime` stopped with \"unconverted data remains\". `fromisoformat` accepts `Z` on Python 3.11+, and this environment runs 3.13.5. No project config sets a minimum Python version.\n\n**Behaviour changes for callers:**\n- **Timezone-aware results:** inputs ending in `Z` now come back with the UTC timezone attached; before, they raised an error. Inputs without a timezone still come back without one, as `test_naive` expects. In Python, comparing or subtracting a datetime with a timezone and one without raises `TypeError`, so watch any code that mixes the two.\n- **Other UTC offsets:** an offset like `+02:00` is now accepted and kept as given; it is not converted to UTC. So `day_key` returns the date in the timestamp's own offset. If the feed can send non-UTC offsets and you want UTC days, add `.astimezone(timezone.utc)` for timezone-aware values.\n- **Looser input:** other ISO-8601 forms, such as a bare date `2026-10-12` or fractional seconds, now parse too instead of raising."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":547,"cacheRead":25494,"cacheWrite":1336,"totalTokens":27379,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":1336}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277416893,"responseId"